  "verdict": "SEV-SNP (Secure Encrypted Virtualization \u2013 Secure Nested Paging) is implemented on AMD's **EPYC server processors**, beginning with the **Zen 3 generation** (EPYC 7003 \"Milan,\" launched 2021), and carried forward in Zen 4 (EPYC 9004 \"Genoa\"/\"Bergamo\") and Zen 5 (EPYC 9005 \"Turin\"). It also appears on EPYC Embedded parts derived from those server dies.\n\n**It has never shipped on consumer Ryzen desktop, mobile, or APU parts.** Consumer and Ryzen PRO chips offer related but distinct memory-encryption features\u2014such as TSME/SME (transparent full-memory encryption)\u2014but the SEV family, including SEV-ES and SEV-SNP, is fused off or absent outside the EPYC line. Confidential-VM features on client hardware instead rely on other mechanisms (e.g., Microsoft Pluton, virtualization-based security).",
